  "independently_generated_insights": [
    "Independence depends on information access and provenance rather than an instruction to ignore known AstroHD information.",
    "Mapping is interpretable only if construct boundaries and reliability analysis cannot move in response to mapping evidence.",
    "Reliability, mapping, and incremental value require separate evidence identities and stopping logic.",
    "A null mapping remains informative only if the original construct and result cannot be repaired away.",
    "A future construct-specific existing-work review belongs after independent definition and before bespoke content.",
    "Source choice can leak a hoped-for mapping and therefore requires provenance and exposure state.",
    "A model session is not chart-blind when contaminated retrieval, history, repository context, or fit-selected examples are present.",
    "Post-exposure revision requires a new exploratory version and new evidence rather than overwriting confirmatory failure."
